WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:03.102
JEANNE MOOS: The city
of Amarillo, Texas,

00:00:03.203 --> 00:00:06.805
is asking folks to guess,
what is this thing?

00:00:06.906 --> 00:00:11.311
The image was captured
last month at 1:25 AM

00:00:11.411 --> 00:00:15.214
by a camera set up
inside the Amarillo Zoo,

00:00:15.315 --> 00:00:17.783
looking out through
a perimeter fence.

00:00:17.884 --> 00:00:19.886
"Is it a person
with a strange hat

00:00:19.986 --> 00:00:21.321
who likes to walk at night?"

00:00:21.421 --> 00:00:26.425
city officials asked in a
tweet, referring to it as a UAO.

00:00:26.526 --> 00:00:29.028
- The unidentified
Amarillo object.

00:00:29.129 --> 00:00:30.396
- Wow.

00:00:30.497 --> 00:00:34.466
JEANNE MOOS: Let the guesses
begin, from Fantastic Mr. Fox--

00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:36.936
- I don't wanna live
in a hole anymore.

00:00:37.037 --> 00:00:41.407
JEANNE MOOS: --to Rocket Raccoon
from "Guardians of the Galaxy."

00:00:41.508 --> 00:00:44.010
- Oh, yeah.

00:00:44.110 --> 00:00:46.679
JEANNE MOOS: The camera is
motion-activated and sends

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:49.882
an alert to zoo officials
when it captures something,

00:00:49.983 --> 00:00:52.451
there were some
serious theories.

00:00:52.552 --> 00:00:54.620 line:8%
MICHAEL KASHUBA: The raccoon
standing on its hind legs

00:00:54.721 --> 00:00:57.389 line:8%
or potentially a person
walking through the park

00:00:57.490 --> 00:01:02.195 line:8%
that just happened to get
captured in a peculiar way.

00:01:02.295 --> 00:01:05.031
JEANNE MOOS: But the public's
guesses were more colorful,

00:01:05.131 --> 00:01:07.467
from Sonic the
Hedgehog to the San

00:01:07.567 --> 00:01:10.036
Antonio Spurs coyote mascot.

00:01:12.639 --> 00:01:15.875
Someone tweeted the movie
"Dog Soldiers called

00:01:15.975 --> 00:01:18.111
and want their werewolf back."

00:01:21.181 --> 00:01:24.417 line:8%
Another poster wondered,
"Is this guy on the loose?"

00:01:24.517 --> 00:01:27.486 line:8%
And, of course, there were
references to Bigfoot,

00:01:27.587 --> 00:01:29.355 line:8%
though someone
thought Littlefoot

00:01:29.456 --> 00:01:31.557 line:14%
might be more appropriate.

00:01:31.658 --> 00:01:34.527
There is no video,
just this image.

00:01:34.627 --> 00:01:37.830
One poster went all out to
illustrate his theory it was

00:01:37.931 --> 00:01:41.901
a "coyote jumping the fence,"
diagrammed with anatomy

00:01:42.001 --> 00:01:44.103
like ears, tail, et cetera.

00:01:44.204 --> 00:01:45.137
Noted.

00:01:45.238 --> 00:01:47.606
If nothing else,
all these guesses

00:01:47.707 --> 00:01:49.341
could leave folks howling.

00:01:49.442 --> 00:01:51.211
[howling]

00:01:52.112 --> 00:01:56.015
Jeanne Moos, CNN, New York.

